You implement task T4 of a Lean 4 proof: the kernel renaming bisimulation of the ERN memory model (owner decision of 2026-11-06 on StaticsOK point (b): "les propriétés prouvées ne changent pas si l'on renomme les identifiants de façon cohérente", in the form of a kernel bisimulation between two StaticsOK numberings, K renamed and read extensionally; the owner accepted the hypothesis that K.Satisfiable is invariant under permutation of footprint, anchor and pin-leaf lists, formalized as `KExt` in the foundation).

Repo /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern; Lean project formal/ (Lean v4.35.0, NO Mathlib), lake at ~/.elan/bin/lake. Follow AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md: docstrings cite spec locations (specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md: §49 last paragraph plus §69/§70/§71 items) and never restate spec text; never sorry/admit/axiom/native_decide; never edit an existing file (only your new file); if a proof is stuck, stop and report the goal state, never weaken a statement. No commits, no git state changes. Lines ≤ 100 characters.

Read first, completely:
- the design: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri--claude-spares-spare-IF4EaH/b714fc3e-3648-484e-9e36-92ef9596c59b/scratchpad/rename-design.md (sections 1–4, 6, 7; risks R7, R9, R11, R12 concern you: FreeCompat's `auth` is NOT renamed (§70.2), alloc shapes are NOT renamed, Satisfiable of k.rename is existential over related states and only the backward direction needs KExt);
- the foundation API already built (formal/Ern/MemoryModel/Access/Rename/{Basic,Places,Derived}.lean): scratchpad/rename-foundation-api.md (same directory). Pitfall: inside a declaration named `SRel.foo`, short names resolve to `SRel.*` first; write kernel names in full (`Access.effective`, `Access.parentOf`, …). `optionRel_trans` needs `(r := …) (r' := …) (r'' := …)` explicitly. Lemmas about Holder.ren/Place.ren/KernelOp.ren live in namespace `Rename`.
- the definitions in formal/Ern/MemoryModel/Access/Ops.lean for §69 endUse (cleanup, endUseS, endUseEff, EndingLeaf, IsRootOf, EndUseAccessOK, EndUseAnchorOK, EndUsePre, EndUseKeptDesc if present), §70 free (OwnedRoot, FreedPlace, freeS, freeEff, FreedLeaf, FreeAccessOK, FreeAnchorOK, FreePre), §71 alloc (AllocStatic, allocP, allocEff, AllocStep with its fail outcome), and KernelOp/KernelOp.Step in Main.lean; existing lemmas in Access/Lemmas.lean, Preserve/EndFree.lean, Preserve/Alloc.lean.

YOUR FILE (new, only this one): formal/Ern/MemoryModel/Access/Rename/OpsEndFree.lean, module Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Rename.OpsEndFree, `import Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Rename.Derived`, new names in namespace Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Rename. Five other agents write sibling files (OpsSmall, OpsTransfer, OpsFrames, Invariants, Init) in parallel: keep helper names specific to your operations, or `private`. Never edit Basic/Places/Derived; put any missing generic helper in your file.
Export per design §4.2 (cleanup/endUse/free/alloc rows, satisfiable_ren): the Pre_ren iffs (general for any k k' with KCorr π α k k' where K appears), Eff_ren, Eff_down, and the contract for the assembly task:
  * `endUse_corr (hS : Sim π α s s') : StepCorr π α (EndUseStep k p s) (EndUseStep (k.rename π α) (π.f p) s')`;
  * `free_corr (hS : Sim π α s s') : StepCorr π α (FreeStep k p auth s) (FreeStep (k.rename π α) (π.f p) auth s')`;
  * `alloc_corr (hk : KExt k) (hS : Sim π α s s') : StepCorr π α (AllocStep k pr ow ls s) (AllocStep (k.rename π α) (π.f pr) (π.f ow) ls s')` (adapt to the exact argument order; reject/fail/ok all correspond);
  * `endUse_down`, `free_down`, `alloc_down : Down s → <Step> s (.ok t) → Down t` (any k);
  * `endUse_sib`, `free_sib`, `alloc_sib (hP : PRel π s.P s'.P) : SibMono π s.P → <Step> s (.ok t) → SibMono π t.P` (any k).
Check iteratively with `cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/MemoryModel/Access/Rename/OpsEndFree.lean`; at the end run `~/.elan/bin/lake build Ern.MemoryModel.Access.Rename.OpsEndFree` once. Do not edit formal/Ern.lean.
Write the exact exported statements to scratchpad/rename-T4-api.md. Final answer: file, exported API path, deviations from the design with reasons, anything unproven with the goal state, `#print axioms` of the three _corr theorems (allowed: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound), build result.

tools.description:
Open the Browser pane: pass `url` to open a browser tab at a URL (no dev server needed — use this for external sites, staging, docs, or your deployed app), OR pass `name` to start a dev server from .claude/launch.json.

Start a dev server by name from .claude/launch.json. If .claude/launch.json doesn't exist, create it first with this format:
{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "<unique-name>",
      "runtimeExecutable": "<command>",
      "runtimeArgs": ["<args>"],
      "port": <port>
    }
  ]
}
Set "runtimeExecutable" to the command (e.g. "npm"), "runtimeArgs" to the arguments (e.g. ["run", "dev"]), and "port" to the server port. An optional "url" (http/https) opens the preview there instead of http://localhost:<port>. A localhost "url" must be just the server's origin — no path or query, matching the entry's port — for example "https://localhost:8443" or "http://app.localhost:3000"; to show a specific page, navigate after the preview opens. Non-localhost URLs may carry paths and are subject to the user's permission and the organization's browsing policy. A configuration with "url" and no command attaches to an already-running server. Only include servers you actually need to preview. Reuses the server if already running. ALWAYS use this instead of Bash for running servers. If the deliverable is already published as an Artifact, update the Artifact instead of starting a server to show it.

